  {
   "slug": "gram:wa-ga-wa",
   "variants": [],
   "steps_unavailable": "Multi-slot clause template, not a derivation from one base. The record's formation is the schema [X]は [Y]が [predicate1]、[Z]は [predicate2]: it places particles across two independent clauses and binds three noun slots plus two predicates. A linear step list transforms exactly one base and can only suffix tokens to it, so any sequence emitted here would collapse to 'noun + は' and would license every は-sentence as this contrast pattern. The record's own explanation field is additionally damaged — two different, conflicting descriptions (the は…が…は contrast frame and the 象は鼻が長い topic/sub-subject frame) are spliced together mid-sentence — so the point needs human repair before steps can be derived.",
   "nuance_tags": [
    "comparison",
    "emphasis"
   ],
   "usage_contexts": [
    "spoken",
    "written"
   ]
  },
